hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  video I'm going to answer a question  from one of our readers Diana who was  asking me what she should major in at  college so she wrote in asking hello I'm  a subscriber to your newsletter and I  really enjoy them thank you I wanted to  know if you have any advice for me I'm a  college student with a passion for  design and business I already have sales  experience and love the business  industry I just can't decide what to  major in I was thinking of event  planning and majoring in business  management do you think it's an  enjoyable and lucrative occupation any  tips anything would be helpful maybe  other job ideas Thank You Diana so Diana  a couple things for you here in terms of  is it enjoyable to be in the event  management business that's completely up  to you right we all have different  things that we like and don't like I  know for me I wouldn't enjoy being an  event planner but for you it could be  the best thing ever so I'd really  encourage you to follow what you're  super passionate about and that will  lead you down the road of success in  terms of it being a lucrative career or  not the amount of money that you make as  an entrepreneur will be in direct  proportion how much value you can add to  your customers so look at the event  management business look at the types of  customers you're dealing with if you see  an opportunity for you to come in and  solve a real problem and add a lot of  value to helping your customers then  you'll be on your way to setting up a  very lucrative type of company in terms  of what to study in school business  management could be great it'll teach  you some of the skills that you need to  run your business I would definitely  look to see if there was an  entrepreneurship course or a small  business course you can sign up for what  I found really helpful when I was in  university was I partnered up with one  of my university professors and I  created my own course so at the time I  had my own business already and wanted  to use the resources of the university a  little bit to help me grow my business  because as an entrepreneur you want to  use everything you can to get your  business forward  so I partnered up with him and we  created our own course design and a lot  of it was around helping my business  grow and he supported that concept and  gave me a mark at the end of it and  there's no final exam which is fantastic  so I would love to see if you could  partner up with one of your professors  and create your own course to help you  grow a business  on top of that to see if event-planning  this for you or not I try to start my  own business part time and take on a  couple clients and see if you'd like  doing the business see if you're really  good at it see if you can add a lot of  value to your customers or partner up  with an event management business offer  your services on a part-time basis and  see if you enjoy doing it talk to the  owner try to add as much value as you  can try to be involved in the business  as much as you can and that way when you  are ready to start your own business you  have experience you know if you like it  or not you know you're really good at  and you're kind of hitting the ground  running so I hope that helps Diana if  you guys liked the video please give it  a thumbs up below and I'd also love to  hear thoughts and feedback if you want  to leave a comment underneath the video  and stay tuned for next episode
 

